    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"lost_negative_case\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"The displayed sources show that participant experience is mainly driven by institutional procedures and formal paperwork.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_95d06119b6dcf0c2\",\"quote\":\"Government could have provided phones.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"The evidence does not present a counterargument regarding the primary drivers of participant experience.\",\"mechanism\":\"Failure to acknowledge alternative factors influencing participant experience.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim oversimplifies the drivers of participant experience, ignoring potential impacts of health crises and individual circumstances.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The evidence highlights concerns about disease spread, fear of infection, and the impact of curfews, suggesting these were significant factors.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The claim makes a broad assertion without considering the diverse experiences and concerns expressed in the provided evidence, particularly regarding health-related anxieties and practical challenges.\"}",
